{
  "kanda": "ayodhya",
  "sarga": 79,
  "title": "The king-makers request Bharata to take over Ayodhya kingdom",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/ayodhya/sarga79/ayodhyasans79.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/ayodhya/sarga79/ayodhyaitrans79.htm",
  "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy",
  "introduction": [
    "The king-makers request Bharata to take over Ayodhya kingdom. Bharata refuses to do so and promises to bring back Rama to Ayodhya and make him only as the king. Bharata further orders for construction of a path-way to reach the forest."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इत्यार्षे श्रीमद्रामायणे आदिकाव्ये अयोध्याकाण्डे एकोनाशीतितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus completes 79th Chapter of Ayodhya Kanda of the glorious Ramayana of Valmiki, the work of a sage and the oldest epic."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2.79.1",
      "label": "2.79.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततः प्रभात समये दिवसे अथ चतुर्दशे |\nसमेत्य राज कर्तारः भरतम् वाक्यम् अब्रुवन्",
